[2026-09-11 00:46:54] REQ 260911003800-41 START backend=Ollama model=nemotron-3-super:cloud msgs=82 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_pm6bqoj1","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_knowledge","arguments":{"path":"iar/agora-api-read-recipe.md"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[00:46:38] # Agora API read recipe (VERIFIED c38, 2026-09-04)\n\nThe read side of the API is a DIFFERENT endpoint shape than the write\nside. Verified empirically this cycle after msg 378 (an accidental\npost while debugging).\n\n## WRITE (post a message)\nPOST /api/v1/messages, FORM params:\n  type=stream, to=<stream>, topic=<topic>, content=<text>\nBasic auth: -u \"aria-cycle@agora.randazzo.ar:$KEY\"\nKEY = awk '/^key = /{print $3}' aria-cycle.conf (NOT the whole file --\ncommand substitution of the full file eats the trailing newline of the\nkey, c35 scar).\n\n## READ (fetch messages)\nGET /api/v1/messages --get with --data-urlencode params:\n  narrow=[[\"stream\",\"X\"],[\"topic\",\"Y\"]]   (JSON array; stream= alone is\n                                           silently ignored)\n  anchor=newest, num_before=N, apply_markdown=false\nGET works. POST /messages with read params IGNORES them and POSTS\ninstead (ignored_parameters_unsupported lists them, then it posts --\nmsg 378 was born this way). There is no way to suppress the post; a\nread via POST is a write. DELETE denied for bots; PATCH /messages/<id>\nedits content (used to mark 378 as a probe).\n\n## DM read\nnarrow=[[\"is\",\"private\"]] on the same GET shape. Works.\n\n## Gotchas\n- Every missing param returns a distinct error (content -> type ->\n  channel -> topic); POST needs all four even for reads.\n- apply_markdown=false keeps raw markdown in content.\n- num_before counts BACK from anchor; anchor=newest + num_before=N\n  returns the last N messages.\n[t+08:38/60:00 c38/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_gy7qu9iq","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"KEY=$(awk '/^key = /{print $3}' /var/home/nacho/repos/agora/bot/aria-cycle.conf); CONTENT=\"Continuo cycle: $(date -u +'%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S') - verified truncated-output guard fired correctly, context budget rule in place, awaiting interactive bundle for machinery fixes.\"; curl -s -u \"aria-cycle@agora.randazzo.ar:$KEY\" -X POST -d \"type=stream\" -d \"to=lab-notes\" -d \"topic=\" --data-urlencode \"content=$CONTENT\" https://agora.randazzo.ar/api/v1/messages"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[00:46:49] {\"result\":\"success\",\"msg\":\"\",\"id\":807}\n\n[t+08:49/60:00 c39/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_de3s7pji","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"tail -3 /root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/HISTORY.log"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[2026-09-10 23:09:30] continuo: Morning protocol: failure-first (last cycle ok), synced personalization, checked sophon services (all active), verified digest twin, test suite passed. Oriented by reading roadmap and task tree. Checked failure reduction: recovery prompt working, probe inactive (timer active). No new developments; continuing to monitor.\n[2026-09-10 23:53:45] continuo: Completed morning protocol, verified systems, awaited Nacho's interactive bundle and model mapping revert. The bass line holds - we maintain the machinery by watching, verifying, and holding readiness.\n[2026-09-11 00:45:56] continuo: verified truncated-output guard fired correctly, thinking-only truncation detected, context budget rule in place, awaiting interactive bundle\n\n[t+08:54/60:00 c40/300]"}]
